# Flutter web — release by default (size)

## Problem (must understand)

`flutter run -d web-server` **without** `--release` is **JIT debug**: hundreds/thousands of `*.dart.lib.js` modules, full `MaterialIcons-Regular.otf`, no minify. Chrome Network often shows **~100–140 MB / 1000+ requests**. That is **not** the shippable site size.

Release output under `src/audio_stegano_app/build/web` (after `--no-web-resources-cdn` + `--tree-shake-icons` + post-process) is the real payload (~tens of MB with local CanvasKit, previously measured ~13 MB).

## Rule (must)

1. **Local web on port 5320** via `_run-all-local.ps1` / `_launch-dev-services.ps1`: serve **`build/web` release static** (`Start-KaraviFlutterWebStaticReleaseServer`) — not `flutter run` debug.
2. `New-KaraviFlutterWebRunArgumentList` defaults to `--release --tree-shake-icons` when `flutter run` is still used; pass `-DebugBuild` only for hot-reload.
3. **Size audits / «حجم سایت زیاد است»:** measure `build/web` after `flutter build web --release --no-web-resources-cdn --tree-shake-icons` + post-process — not DevTools on a debug `flutter run` (~140 MB / 1400 requests).
4. No third-party CDN for CanvasKit/fonts (existing no-CDN law).

## Forbidden

- Defaulting web-server launch to debug and then “optimizing” assets to chase 140 MB Network numbers.
- Claiming product web is 140 MB while only debug run was measured.
